Infra setup checklist — Istio ambient, namespace-by-namespace enablement

 

Install (one-time)
- Install Istio ambient profile — istiod + ztunnel DaemonSet (all nodes) + istio-cni
- Do not deploy sidecar-injection; no istio-injection labels anywhere
- Confirm Gateway API CRDs v1 exist and are owned by Envoy Gateway (Istio ships none — don't add conflicting ones)
- Ensure istio-waypoint GatewayClass is registered, and istiod's Gateway deployment controller is enabled
- Keep istio-cni excluded namespaces to only kube-system and istio-system
- Leave ambient.dnsCapture: true (default) enabled
- Do not apply any cluster-wide AuthorizationPolicy, PeerAuthentication (leave PERMISSIVE), or root-namespace Telemetry
- Do not manage/overwrite the istio.io/dataplane-mode namespace label — that stays ours

 

CA / identity
- State the CA mode (istiod self-signed, cert-manager-istio-csr, or plug-in), trust domain = cluster.local, and workload cert lifetime = 24h
- If using istio-csr: include istio-system/ztunnel in caTrustedNodeAccounts
- Confirm workload cert issuance + rotation is working and monitored

 

Waypoint support
- Apply the istio-waypoint defaults ConfigMap in istio-system (key gateway.istio.io/defaults-for-class: istio-waypoint): HPA min 2 / max 5 @ 70% CPU, PDB minAvailable: 1, resources 300m/512Mi → 3/2Gi
- Ensure metrics-server is installed (waypoint HPA needs it)
- Don't strip Prometheus scrape annotations (prometheus.io/scrape, :15020, /stats/prometheus) from generated waypoint pods

 

Telemetry
- Keep ztunnel :15020 metrics scrapeable (prometheus.io annotations intact) — we scrape into SigNoz

 

RBAC (grant to our pipeline service connection)
- In our app namespaces: create/update/delete AuthorizationPolicy, Telemetry, Gateway (class istio-waypoint); label namespaces (istio.io/dataplane-mode, istio.io/use-waypoint)
- In istio-system: read ztunnel metrics (or provide scrape path), create ServiceEntry later
- Read access: pods, logs, events

 

Operations
- Give us the addon change/upgrade notice (we byte-compare pinned renders)
- Roll out istio-cni to nodes canaried/progressively, not all-at-once

